WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.033
- [Instructor] In this video,

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.370
we're going to try to figure out

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:07.250
what 4/10 divided by five is.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.950
So pause this video and see
if you can think about it

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.400
before we work through it together.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.440
We're really going to think
about approaching this visually.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.430
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:21.520
Let's actually try to think
about what 4/10 looks like.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.470
So if you view this
entire square as a whole,

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.750
you see that we've divided
it into 10 equal columns

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:32.070
or 10 equal sections,
and four of those tenths

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:37.070
are shaded in, so what you
see here in blue is 4/10.

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:41.630
But how do we divide that into
five and make sense of it?

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:43.130
Well, one way to think about it

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:47.030
is to imagine 4/10 not just as 4/10,

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:50.350
but to imagine it as 40/100,

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.830
so this would be imagining it as 40/100.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.620
So we can re-write 4/10 divided by 5

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:01.083
as 40/100 divided by 5,

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:06.860
and now we can think about
taking these 40 hundredths,

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.680
each of these little
squares is a hundredth,

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.640
and divide it into five equal sections,

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.660
and then we can say,
well, how many hundredths

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:17.400
are in each of those five equal sections?

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.520
So let's do that.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:23.520
So let's see, this is one, this is two,

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:29.090
this is three, this is four

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:31.740
and then we have five equal sections.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:36.120
So how many hundredths are in
each of those equal sections?

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.870
Well we can see in each of them you have

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:42.400
one, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.520
So 40/100 divided by five

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.730
is going to be 8/100, because
we have eight of these

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.570
little squares in each of
those five equal sections.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:56.240
So 8/100 we would like this.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.950
And so 40/100 divided by five is 8/100,

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:04.950
then 4/10 divided by five
is also equal to 8/100.

